Subject: [M152] Keep transceiver MID in sync with its channel

Original change's description:
> Keep transceiver MID in sync with its channel
>
> When applying a local description, a transceiver could be matched to an
> m= section by its index even if it was already associated with a
> different MID. The channel of the transceiver keeps using the MID it was
> created for, so the two could get out of sync.
>
> - Only match transceivers that are not yet associated by m= section
>   index.
> - Route transport changes to a transceiver based on the MID of its
>   channel.
>
> Bug: chromium:567160162
